    "title": "Will Marshalls Be Open on Easter Sunday 2025?",
    "text": "Much like its off-price sister store T.J.Maxx, Marshalls is a one-stop shop for all the things. No, you can't buy eggs and milk there, but you can scoop up clothing, toys, home decor, kitchen gear, shoes and even beauty products at the store. It's truly a mecca for bargain hunting when you're not totally sure what you need, but you know you need (or want) something. So is Marshalls open on Easter?If, like so many of us, you have a even the tiniest bit of procrastinator in you, chances are you could be relying on Marshalls for last-minute Easter goodies. After all, there's always room left in those baskets for a little something extra. Or maybe you just realized your kid has already outgrown their dress shoes they were supposed to wear for Easter brunch. The spur of the moment holiday needs are endless, and Marshalls' Easter hours could really come in handy.SIGN UP for the Dengarden / Parade Home & Garden newsletter for a weekly dose of our favorite house hacks, decor trends and shopping dealsIs Marshalls Open on Easter Sunday?It's the question of the moment—will Marshalls have store hours on Easter. The answer is no, Marshalls isn't open on Easter. In fact, none of the stores that full under TJX Companies will be open on the Sunday holiday. This includes T.J.Maxx, HomeGoods, Homesense and Sierra.This may be a bummer for would-be Easter Sunday shoppers, but closing stores allows employees time to spend with their families and loved ones. Which, in retail, is hard to come by as it seems like stores are always open in an attempt to satisfy customer demand.Related: This Home Decor TikToker Just Made the Easiest Easter Centerpiece—\"Such a Creative Idea!\"So make sure those dress shoes fit the day before Easter, as Marshalls will be open the Saturday prior so you have until store close (hours vary by location) to get any last-minute items.And if you're really in a bind, there are still some stores that will be open on Easter Sunday to help out with basket fillers and holiday meal needs. Look to groceries to have reduced hours that day, as well as pharmacies like CVS and Walgreens, which will both be open.But, also, maybe take a cue from these retailers and just relax on Easter Sunday, appreciating time with the people you care about. And, hey, those extra chocolate eggs will be marked down by Monday, so, really, you're winning.Related: Aldi Just Dropped the Most Adorable Spring Find and It's Perfect for Easter",
